esult\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-0\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram II shows three points that are <em>not</em> collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-1\"></div>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-155031-e-2\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-155031-e-2\"></div>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
